      "writtenOn": "2025-11-04T01:19:58Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I see that other codecs provide an API that allows their clients to specify if the input is a BMP vs BMP-embedded-in-ICO:\n\n* `SkBmpCodec::MakeFromStream` and `SkBmpCodec::MakeFromIco`\n* `blink::BMPImageReader(..., bool is_in_ico)`\n* [`pub(crate) fn new_with_ico_format`](https://github.com/image-rs/image/blob/3dba2bd6e1e783974cce6e011a6e55be681ddcd3/src/codecs/bmp/decoder.rs#L545) vs public [`BmpDecoder::new`](https://docs.rs/image/latest/image/codecs/bmp/struct.BmpDecoder.html#method.new)\n\nI wonder if we can discuss our longer-term plans for BMP-in-ICO:\n\n* Option 1: Ship `SkBmpRustCodec` itself first.\n    - Option 1a: Provide API that `SkIcoCodec` can use to use `SkBmpRustCodec` instead of `SkBmpCodec`\n    - Option 1b: Continue shipping `SkIcoCodec` built on top of `SkBmpCodec`\n* Option 2: Postpone shipping `SkBmpRustCodec` until it can ship together with `SkIcoRustCodec` (potentially handling ICO \u003d\u003e BMP handoff in the Rust layer, without any C++-level APIs for ICO handling)\n\nOnce we settle on a plan, it would be great to capture that in a TODO comment (or if longer description is needed, then in a bug).",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 25,
        "startChar": 32,
        "endLine": 25,
        "endChar": 62
      },
      "revId": "cc6e7f648b2c05b805a99333be3bfdfea2dcc491",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
