      "writtenOn": "2025-11-04T01:19:58Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This manual calculation looks okay, but I think it can be avoided by using `SkPixmap`:\n\n```\n// At the top of the method:\nSkPixmap dstPixmap(dstInfo, dst, dstRowStride);\n\n// And then here:\nuint8_t* dstRow \u003d dstPixmap.writable_addr8(0, y);\n```\n\n(I think it would be great if `SkPixmap` could be potentially extended with `writable_row8(int y)` API that returns `SkSpan\u003cuint8_t\u003e`.  That seems like something that could be done in a separate CL.  OTOH maybe this requires a more strategic approach to span-ification of Skia.)",
      "range": {
