      "message": "IIUC this `else` block can execute when `dstRow` is (say) `kGray_8_SkColorType`.  In this case, `memcpy` would be incorrect.  AFAIU the legacy `SkBmpCodec` [uses](https://source.chromium.org/chromium/chromium/src/+/main:third_party/skia/src/codec/SkBmpStandardCodec.cpp;l\u003d227;drc\u003d35d26d364efb57d0386b98312ba739f7f65ae97e) `SkSwizzler` to handle all the pixel format transformations.  I think using `SkSwizzler` would also let us avoid the manual BGR/RGB -\u003e RGB_565 and RGBA/BGRA transformations on lines 186-260.",
