      "writtenOn": "2025-11-04T22:12:30Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Optional: I don\u0027t have a strong opinion, but WDYT about directly replicating the whole `BITMAPV5HEADER` as a `#[repr(C)]` `struct` in Rust - this would give the offset and the field definition for free.  And `bytemuck` should help with transmuting `\u0026[u8]` to `\u0026BitmapV5Header` (I think this can be done without using `unsafe impl` or other `unsafe` - `#[derive(AnyBitPattern)]` should help with this).\n\nBenefit of doing this: more direct link to the original definition/documentation of the BMP header structs / less magical constants like 123 or 56.\n\nDownside of doing this: have to spell all the fields, even ones that are unused.\n\nBut as I said, I don\u0027t feel strongly about this.",
