      "side": 1,
      "message": "Optional alternative spelling:\n\n`u32::from_le_bytes(slice[30..33].try_into().unwrap())`\n\n`try_into` converts `\u0026[u8]` into `Option\u003c[u8; 4]\u003e` depending on whether the input slice has the right length.  And then `unwrap` gets `[u8; 4]`.\n\n------\n\nFWIW the `png` crate has its own helper trait [here](https://source.chromium.org/chromium/chromium/src/+/main:third_party/rust/chromium_crates_io/vendor/png-v0_18/src/traits.rs;l\u003d27-41;drc\u003d128f35b3fb019f2fa67e1e798e113ed95f766096) (usage example [here](https://source.chromium.org/chromium/chromium/src/+/main:third_party/rust/chromium_crates_io/vendor/png-v0_18/src/decoder/stream.rs;l\u003d1319-1327;drc\u003d28aa32fee5483719888905c78bcd54649a8c8c8d)).\n\nAnd the `image` crate uses the `byteorder_lite` crate and its `read_u32` helper: https://docs.rs/byteorder-lite/latest/byteorder_lite/trait.ReadBytesExt.html#method.read_u32",
