      "writtenOn": "2025-11-04T22:12:30Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "One high-level/design concern here is that the target color space (in `const SkImageInfo\u0026 dstInfo` passed to `SkCodec` APIs like [`getImage`](https://source.chromium.org/chromium/chromium/src/+/main:third_party/skia/include/codec/SkCodec.h;l\u003d444-445;drc\u003d82de95a10c9db0d1d59de4a6db75ffd41bc93d81)) is not always sRGB IIUC.  In particular, a user may have calibrated their local display differently.\n\nI wonder if it would be possible to instead:\n\n1. Continue (from the current `SkPngRustCodec` and the future/WIP `SkPngBmpCodec`) using Skia for actual color space transformations (i.e. `skcms` / `SkCodec::applyColorXform` / maaaybe also somehow reusing `SkSwizzler`+`ColorXform` combo provided by `SkPngCodecBase`)\n2. Put together a separate/prerequisite CL to:\n    * Try creating a new internal Skia API for using Rust/`moxcms` for parsing `\u0026[u8]` / `SkSpan\u003cconst uint8_t\u003e` into `SkEncodedInfo::ICCProfile`\n    * Using this parser from `SkPngRustCodec`.\n    \nInitial `SkBmpRustCodec` implementation can either:\n\n* Initially parse ICC using native/C++ code (just as the current/old `SkPngRustCodec` code does [here](https://source.chromium.org/chromium/chromium/src/+/main:third_party/skia/src/codec/SkPngRustCodec.cpp;l\u003d158-169;drc\u003d5658e91de531f3a05ebb87fad3deed5da7ecb5b2)) use Skia to parse the ICC bytes exposed/provided/decoded from BMP\n* Or use the new internal, Rust-backed parsing from the separate CL suggested above.\n    \nWDYT?",
