      "writtenOn": "2025-11-04T22:12:30Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I am not sure if/how my feedback here is actionable, but it seems to me that `Rle8`-vs-`Rle4` difference is not necessarily something that the decoder client needs to know about.\n\nMy first reaction to that was to ask if `CompressionType` needs to be `pub`-lic.  And that would cascade into a question if `BmpHeaderInfo` needs to be `pub`-lic (vs crate-internal).  This doesn\u0027t matter that much at this point (where `rust_bmp/.../*.rs` is just an internal implementation detail of Skia), but would matter in the long-term if/when we want to extract this crate out of Skia and publish as a separate crate.\n\nI think that the decoder client wants to know what kind of pixel format will/can come out of the decoder - maybe the API can be built around that?  I don\u0027t know what is supported by the BMP format - RGBA8 and RGB8?  And also BGRA8 and BGR8?  Is palette-index also a possible output (I know that `SkSwizzler` can accept that as input and efficiently transform into RGBA)?  Is gray-scale also a possible output?  Is something like RGBA-16bits or RGBA-4bits or RGB-5-6-5 also a possible output?\n\nPS. IIUC the `image` crate uses the `ColorType` enum for this.  This seems a little bit incomplete (e.g. it can\u0027t represent \"indexed\" output from a PNG decoder), but maybe this is good enough for BMP?  `ColorType` doesn\u0027t explicitly cover BGRA, but we could in theory cover this with some extra copies :-/.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 50,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 51,
        "endChar": 9
      },
